# CreditBubble: Private Credit Stress Intelligence System
## Initial Specification — May 2026

---

## INTENT

This system replicates the analytical process used by top fixed-income trading desks (e.g., Millennium, Citadel) to systematically read SEC filings across the private credit universe and identify stress signals before they are widely recognized. The goal is to generate actionable long/short trading signals by detecting deterioration in private credit fund books — specifically Business Development Companies (BDCs) and alternative asset managers — using publicly available data that most investors do not systematically process.

The core thesis: private credit funds mark illiquid assets quarterly using internal models with every incentive to be optimistic. Stress signals appear in the filings many quarters before a fund cuts its distribution, caps redemptions, or faces a regulatory investigation. The BlackRock TCP Capital DOJ investigation (May 2026) is an example of the endpoint; this system is designed to find the beginning.

